Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Raydhanji of Adhoi and Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s Divine Strength Once, Shriji Maharaj graced the village of Adhoi in Kutch and resided in the darbar of Ladhaji for two months. There, Maharaj engaged in scriptural debates with Kabirpanthis and refuted their tenets. Ladhaji had four sons: Adoji, Kalyanji, Ramsangji, and Raydhanji. Shriji Maharaj stayed at their residence, performed numerous divine lilas, and bestowed divine bliss upon everyone.
One day, Maharaj was seated upon a cot, and the four brothers sat reverently before Him. Shri Hari asked, &ldquo;You are four brothers; who among you is the strongest?&rdquo;
The three brothers replied, &ldquo;Raydhanji is exceptionally strong. He can break eight coconuts simultaneously—placing two under his armpits, two inside his elbows, two between his thighs and lower abdomen, and two between his calves and thighs; standing up and then sitting down with force, he shatters all eight coconuts at once! He can snap a fourfold thick rope tied around his knees in a single thrust, and when in full vigor, he can crush an areca nut to powder between his fingertips just like a nutcracker.&rdquo;
Hearing this, Shriji Maharaj said to Raydhanji, &ldquo;Grip Our wrist.&rdquo;
Raydhanji hesitated and said, &ldquo;Maharaj! Your holy body has become very lean due to severe austerities. It would not be proper for me to grip Your wrist.&rdquo;
Maharaj reassured him, &ldquo;Do not worry about Us; grip Our wrist firmly with all your strength without any fear.&rdquo;
Raydhanji agreed, &ldquo;Very well, Maharaj!&rdquo; Shriji Maharaj extended His right hand, and Raydhanji gripped the wrist with one hand.
Maharaj said, &ldquo;Hold it with both hands.&rdquo; Raydhanji gripped it tightly with both hands.
Maharaj cautioned him repeatedly, &ldquo;Hold tight, beware!&rdquo;
Raydhanji replied, &ldquo;I have held it very firmly.&rdquo;
Then Maharaj effortlessly released His wrist, caught Raydhanji&rsquo;s right hand under His arm, and pressed it. Raydhanji was instantly overcome with intense agony and could not utter a word! Seeing Raydhanji&rsquo;s distressed face, Shriji Maharaj released his hand. Raydhanji sat holding his hand for a long time and groaned, &ldquo;O Maharaj! The bones of my hand are shattered!&rdquo;
Maharaj said, &ldquo;Come here, let Us examine it.&rdquo; When Raydhanji showed his hand, Maharaj inspected it and smiled, &ldquo;The hand is completely intact; no bone is broken.&rdquo;
The four brothers rose and went to sit at a distance. Maharaj asked, &ldquo;Why are you sitting so far away?&rdquo;
Raydhanji folded his hands and submitted, &ldquo;During Krishnavatar, Lord Krishna was only eleven years old when He slew the formidable elephant Kuvalayapida, the mighty wrestlers Chanura and Mushtika, and King Kamsa. We always harbored a doubt in our minds as to how a young boy could accomplish such feats. Today, that doubt has vanished forever! Witnessing Your divine prowess, we realize that You are neither young nor physically frail; You are Aksharatit Purna Purushottam Narayan Himself! Today we have recognized You in truth. O Maharaj! You are not merely one to jest with; You are the supreme Almighty, worthy of eternal adoration and worship.&rdquo; Realizing that Maharaj is the ultimate source of all divine incarnations, all the men and women of the household devoted themselves wholeheartedly to Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s service.
Another day, Shriji Maharaj said to a devotee of Adhoi, &ldquo;We have heard that very fine ghee is prepared at your home.&rdquo; The devotee happily clarified fresh butter from his milch buffaloes, poured a large bronze bowl full of pure ghee, and presented it to Maharaj. Looking at the bowl, Shriji Maharaj asked, &ldquo;The ghee is wonderful; have you given this for Us to drink?&rdquo; The devotee replied, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Please drink it happily.&rdquo; Maharaj raised the bowl to His lips and drank the entire bowl of ghee in one go! When the devotee ran his finger inside the empty bowl, not a single trace of grease adhered to his finger!
The devotee exclaimed in astonishment, &ldquo;Just as in Krishnavatar Putana came to breastfeed You and You sucked away her very life-breath along with the milk, similarly not a hint of oiliness remains in this vessel!&rdquo; Shriji Maharaj chuckled, &ldquo;You offered it for Us to drink, so We drank it.&rdquo; The devotee laughed, &ldquo;O Maharaj! You did not even leave any prasad for us!&rdquo; Hearing this, Maharaj and the devotees laughed heartily.
On another occasion, the mother of the four brothers petitioned Shri Hari with folded hands, &ldquo;O Maharaj! My four sons are devout in worshipping God, but in practical family affairs they do not listen to advice and wish to separate. Lest they quarrel among themselves, whatever division You decide, we shall happily accept.&rdquo; Shriji Maharaj divided the property into four equal lots and drew lots. Each brother received his share happily and returned home, preparing delicious feasts for Shri Hari and pleasing Him through various devotional services.
Raydhanji and the devoted family hosted Shri Hari in their home for two full months. Every day Maharaj bathed in the local river and in the sacred kund on the opposite bank, offering darshan to Shri Pataleshwar Mahadev.
One day, Raydhanji&rsquo;s sister-in-law pleaded with Maharaj, &ldquo;Please do not allow the sadhus to go out begging today; we wish to feed them at home.&rdquo; Maharaj joked, &ldquo;It is better to let them go; otherwise, if they remain hungry, they will complain in the bazaar that they were invited to Raydhanji&rsquo;s house only to be starved!&rdquo; She replied, &ldquo;Complain only if they remain hungry!&rdquo; Eight sadhus and Shriji Maharaj sat down for lunch. Maharaj instructed the sadhus not to refuse any serving. As they served generously, the cooked provisions ran out. Maharaj said, &ldquo;Bring more if there is any!&rdquo; Raydhanji playfully told his sister-in-law, &ldquo;Admit defeat now!&rdquo; She quickly borrowed ghee from a neighbor, but Maharaj laughed, &ldquo;We do not partake of borrowed food from someone else&rsquo;s house!&rdquo; and indulged in joyous divine humor. In this manner, Shri Hari performed countless uplifting lilas in Adhoi.
