Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Rata Basiya of Gadhpur and Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s Divine Humor Shriji Maharaj was gracing Gadhpur with His divine presence. One day, He was presiding over an assembly in the Akshar Ordi. Brahmanand Swami and other revered sadhus, along with noble devotees like Sura Khachar, Somla Khachar, and Dada Khachar, were seated before Him. Just then, Rata Basiya arrived. Seeing him, Shriji Maharaj remarked, &ldquo;This Rata Basiya is Our dear, close friend!&rdquo; Then, turning to him, Maharaj affectionately asked, &ldquo;How are you doing, Rata?&rdquo;
Delighted, Rata replied, &ldquo;Maharaj, today I went to the river! There, I had a fierce fight with my own echo, so I am feeling terribly hungry today!&rdquo; Hearing this innocent reply, Shriji Maharaj called Mulji Brahmachari and instructed him to bring one seer (~half a kilogram) of pure ghee and one seer of sugar for Rata Basiya. Mulji Brahmachari promptly brought it and handed it to Rata, who immediately sat down and began eating it right there in the assembly.
Seeing this, Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s close friend and companion, Sura Khachar, exclaimed, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Why did You give a seer of ghee and a seer of sugar to Rata at this hour? He is completely insane!&rdquo;
Hearing this, Rata Basiya instantly retorted, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Am I insane, and this Sura Khachar is wise? Every morning at home, his wife beats him over the head with slippers, and in his own household, his stature is no more than that of a puppet! Yet here he sits before You, sporting a huge turban, boasting grandly, and calling me crazy!&rdquo;
Hearing this, Brahmanand Swami, who was seated in the assembly, intervened gently, &ldquo;Oh you innocent soul, one should not speak to the Darbar like that! He is an elder chieftain, so one should not address him in that manner.&rdquo;
Upon hearing Swami&rsquo;s words, Rata turned back to Maharaj and said, &ldquo;Maharaj, so I am foolish and your Brahmanand here is wise? He merely takes two poetic lines from here and two from there, and ends every verse with &lsquo;Bhane Brahmanand&rsquo; (Says Brahmanand)! And Maharaj, nowhere in the entire book does he ever mention Your name—he only keeps promoting his own name!&rdquo;
Upon hearing this hilarious and innocent exchange, Shriji Maharaj and the entire assembly burst into hearty laughter. Throughout that day, everyone kept fondly recalling Rata Basiya&rsquo;s endearing banter and laughing heartily, and Shriji Maharaj and all the devotees showered immense divine love and pleasure upon that guileless devotee.
From Shri Haricharitra Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
