Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Vanik Devotee of Dhinkvali and Shriji Maharaj Once, Shriji Maharaj set out from Gadhpur (Gadhada) towards Vadtal along with a large congregation (sangh) of sadhus and devotees. Commencing their journey early in the morning, they passed through the village of Tajpar near Botad and reached the village of Dhinkvali. A devoted Vanik devotee resided in this village. Upon learning of Maharaj&rsquo;s arrival, he came running, intercepted Shri Hari and the devotees along the path, fell prostrate in dandavat pranam, and prayed with folded hands, &ldquo;O Maharaj! You have graced our village along with all the sadhus and devotees; please stay at my home today!&rdquo; Shri Hari replied, &ldquo;The sun is rising higher, the heat is increasing, and we still have a long distance to travel; hence, halting here will not be feasible.&rdquo;
With tears welling up in his eyes, the Vanik devotee pleaded fervently, &ldquo;O Maharaj, please sanctify our home by accepting Thal (sacred meal) today and depart tomorrow morning! And if You are in great haste, then once the afternoon heat subsides, Sarangpur is nearby—You may proceed there and rest for the night. But please grant us the blessed opportunity to serve lunch to everyone this afternoon!&rdquo;
Perceiving the sincere devotion and loving affection in the devotee&rsquo;s heart, Shri Hari said, &ldquo;The other sadhus and devotees of the sangh have already arrived in Sarangpur, so it is necessary for Us to reach there as well. You wish to halt Us in order to serve food; however, walking behind Us are the devotee Kamalshi Sheth and his wife. Kindly stop them, serve them with utmost hospitality and care, and feed them with love. We shall consider that service to be as good as feeding Us directly in person! Therefore, please permit Us to proceed and do not insist any further.&rdquo; Honoring Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s divine wish, the Vanik devotee consented and allowed Maharaj to continue. Deeply pleased with him, Shriji Maharaj proceeded towards Sarangpur.
Later, Kamalshi Sheth and his wife arrived in the village on foot. The Vanik devotee halted them and conveyed, &ldquo;Shriji Maharaj has instructed that both of you must come to our home and rest.&rdquo; Kamalshi Sheth remarked, &ldquo;I was utterly exhausted from walking; Maharaj, knowing the innermost state of my mind, gave you this instruction.&rdquo;
The devotee took Kamalshi Sheth and his wife to his home and showered them with warm hospitality. He prepared warm water for their bath and served them a delicious meal with immense love. When they rested in the afternoon, he massaged their feet (charan-champi) and brought them great comfort and joy.
As the afternoon heat cooled, Kamalshi Sheth and his wife resumed their journey and reached Sarangpur by dusk. Shriji Maharaj was residing for the night in the Darbargadh of Jiva Khachar. Kamalshi Sheth went there, had Maharaj&rsquo;s divine darshan, and narrated in detail how, obeying His command, the Vanik devotee of Dhinkvali had lovingly hosted them, served them, and fed them with great devotion. Hearing this, Shriji Maharaj was immensely delighted and remarked with a gentle smile, &ldquo;He served Our devotee with profound love and fed him so affectionately; now We are forever indebted to that Vanik devotee, and We must surely repay that debt of love!&rdquo;
From Shri Hari Charitra Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
