Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Youth of Zalavad and the Divine Call of Devanand Swami Once, while traveling for Satsang vicharan, Sadguru Devanand Swami arrived at a village in Zalavad. He took up lodging in the village square (choro). In the evening, after the sacred aarti at the Ramji temple, Swami delivered spiritual discourses (katha) and divine teachings. Deeply touched by his profound saintliness, the spiritual seekers (mumukshus) of the village requested him to stay longer.
Swami ate only once a day and awakened spiritual consciousness wherever he went through his sublime teachings and soul-stirring kirtans brimming with detachment (vairagya). Every evening, the gathering at the spiritual assembly continued to grow. Inspired by Swami’s saintly life and discourses, many villagers renounced harmful addictions, accepted the five sacred vows (vartaman), and embraced Satsang. Swami sanctified that village by staying there for about fifteen to twenty days.
A few days after Swami departed for another village, a young, vibrant son of a devoted devotee suddenly fell critically ill, and his final moments drew near. Lying on his bed, the youth called out to his mother and said, &ldquo;Mother! I am departing for Akshardham! I behold the divine darshan of Shriji Maharaj and His liberated souls (muktas). Our gurudev, Devanand Swami, is also present right beside Him! Swami is telling me, &lsquo;Dear child, get ready to come to the divine abode; we have accompanied Maharaj to take you to Akshardham!&rsquo;&rdquo;
Overcome by maternal attachment, the mother cried out anxiously, &ldquo;Son, pray to Gurudev Devanand Swami: &lsquo;Swami, I do not wish to go to the abode right now!&rsquo;&rdquo; The spiritually enlightened youth replied, &ldquo;Mother, there is no real happiness in this fleeting mortal world. All supreme peace and divine bliss reside solely in the holy murti of Maharaj. Therefore, I wish to depart for Akshardham this very instant.&rdquo;
Surrendering to the divine will, the mother said with deep devotion, &ldquo;Very well, my son. If Shriji Maharaj Himself has come to take you, go with Him happily to the divine abode. But when our guru Devanand Swami visits our village again, I shall surely ask him why he did not even try to stop Shriji Maharaj from taking away my only son!&rdquo;
Offering his humble salutations and greeting everyone with &ldquo;Jai Swaminarayan,&rdquo; the blessed youth departed for Akshardham along with Shriji Maharaj and Sadguru Devanand Swami.
From Shri Haricharitra Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
