Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Boat Ride Across the Narmada and Sura Bapu&rsquo;s Nudge Shri Hari set out from Vadtal to journey toward Surat. Sura Khachar, along with a congregation of santos and devotees, accompanied Him. Upon reaching Bharuch, they came to the sacred Narmada River. To cross over to the opposite bank, everyone boarded a hired boat. Right next to Shri Hari and Sura Bapu sat a stubborn and unruly Vairagi bava. He lit intoxicating datura in his small clay pipe (hokali) and began puffing away, billowing thick clouds of smoke. Shri Hari remained silent and said nothing, but Sura Bapu could not tolerate it. Turning red with indignation and rising in his true Kathi warrior spirit, he snapped, &ldquo;Hey, foolish bava! If you want to blow thick clouds of smoke from that datura, go sit further away and puff all you want there! All of your foul smoke is drifting straight onto my Shriji Maharaj! So move aside and sit at a distance!&rdquo;
The bava acted as if he had heard nothing and completely ignored Sura Bapu. This irked Sura Bapu even more, but since Shri Hari was present, he could not openly engage in a brawl. So, sitting right beside him, Sura Bapu discreetly delivered a solid punch with his fist into the bava’s ribs. The bava began muttering and cursing in anger.
Hearing him grumble, Sura Bapu remarked innocently, &ldquo;Listen, holy Sadhu Mahatma! Why are you losing your temper? Look at me—even I felt anger, but am I getting angry? If you succumb to anger, you will ruin your salvation (kalyan)!&rdquo; Shriji Maharaj held a handkerchief to His mouth and burst into laughter, saying, &ldquo;Sura Bapu! You hit him with a solid punch, and now you are preaching to him not to get angry?!&rdquo;
The boat set sail and began navigating the river’s currents. The bava, still grumbling, once again lit his pipe and started smoking datura. When the smoke drifted toward Sura Bapu and Shri Hari again, Sura Bapu warned him not to smoke, but the bava refused to listen. This time, sitting beside him, Sura Bapu thrust a sharp jab with his elbow. Stung by the blow, the bava leaped up grumbling and retreated all the way to the far corner of the boat to sit down. Shri Hari laughed heartily and said, &ldquo;Sura Bapu, you truly succeeded in making that Mahatma move away!&rdquo;
Sura Khachar replied, &ldquo;O Maharaj! That obstinate fellow wouldn&rsquo;t understand gentle words. The moment I gave him a jab with my elbow, he stood right up and fled! Now he may sit peacefully in that far corner and blow as much smoke as he pleases!&rdquo;
From Shri Hari Charitra Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
